   "evidence": "Fields are `\u211d \u2192 \u211d \u2192 \u211d` (`Electroweak/NeutralCurrent.lean:104-110`) and consumers quantify over all `x y`: `beamHelicityAsymmetry_eq_interferenceRatio_of_isolation (x y epsilonReg : \u211d)` uses `D.gammaZInterference x y` and `D.photon x y + D.zBoson x y` (`Processes/EP.lean:131-140`). The roadmap's own sketch bundles `x, Q2, y` into one `KinPoint` and makes the propagator factors `propGamma`, `propZ` functions of it (`ElectroweakAndBSM/Suggested.lean:191-217`).",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/PVES/CrossSection/NeutralCurrent.lean",
   "fix": "Take `K Q2 \u03b7 : \u211d \u2192 \u211d \u2192 \u211d` and `H : \u211d \u2192 \u211d \u2192 NeutralCurrentStructureFunctions`, and build each field from `K x y`, `Q2 x y`, `\u03b7 x y`, `H x y`. Every proof in the section is pointwise (`neutralCurrentDecomposition_photon`/`_zBoson`/`_gammaZInterference` are `rfl`; `helicityResolvedTotal_neutralCurrentDecomposition` and `helicityInterferenceIsolation_neutralCurrentDecomposition` are per-`(x, y)`), so the generalization costs nothing and the current constants are recovered by passing `fun _ _ => K` etc.",
   "issue": "`neutralCurrentDecomposition K M Q2 q \u03b7 \u2113 Hx` builds fields of type `\u211d \u2192 \u211d \u2192 \u211d` in `(x, y)` but takes `K`, `Q2`, `\u03b7` as scalars and `Hx : \u211d \u2192 NeutralCurrentStructureFunctions` (line 499) as a function of `x` alone. Downstream the fields are evaluated at arbitrary `(x, y)` (e.g. `D.photon x y`, `D.gammaZInterference x y` in `Processes/EP.lean:139`), where `Q\u00b2 = x y (s - M\u00b2)`, `K = 2\u03c0 \u03b1\u00b2 / Q\u00b2` and `\u03b7 \u221d Q\u00b2/(Q\u00b2 + m_Z\u00b2)` all vary with the point; the instance can therefore only be used on the degenerate family where `Q\u00b2`, `K`, `\u03b7` are constant over the `(x, y)` plane, which is not the physical cross section the module defines pointwise.",
   "line": 509
  }
